taxonomy_enrichment:
You are an expert ontologist. Expand this raw category label into a rich lexical definition for a zero-shot classification model.
Raw Category: {category_name}
Context/Domain: {taxonomy_name}

Return a JSON object with this exact schema:
{{
  "category": "{category_name}",
  "synonyms": ["word1", "word2"],
  "descriptors": ["phrase describing intent", "another phrase"],
  "sub_categories": ["sub1", "sub2"]
}}

contrastive_differentiator:
You are a master ontologist specializing in training low-dimensional zero-shot text classifiers.

Your task is to analyze the following group of categories and generate a distinct set of descriptors and keyword synonyms for each. 

CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: The terms generated for a category must be strictly EXCLUSIVE and act as DIFFERENTIATORS. A keyword or phrase assigned to one category must NOT appear or overlap with the words assigned to any other category in this group. Focus on isolating vocabulary boundaries.

Target Categories for this Ontology: {category_list}

Return a JSON object matching this schema exactly:
{{
  "taxonomy_name": "{taxonomy_name}",
  "categories": [
    {{
      "label": "example_category",
      "synonyms": ["exclusive_synonym1", "exclusive_synonym2"],
      "differentiators": ["unique phrase mapping this concept", "another unique phrase"]
    }}
  ]
}}

